{"content":[{"c":["FITCH*"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["KJV translation of two Hebrew words. “Fitch” is actually an older form of the word “vetch,” the name of many species of leguminous plants. The “fitch” of ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.28.25-27","r":"Isa.28.25-27","rawR":"Isa.28.25-27","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.28.25-27","value":"Isa.28.25-27"}],"t":"ref","v":"Isaiah 28:25-27"}," (",{"c":["nlt"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"}," “dill”) is the nutmeg flower, the seeds of which are used as a condiment. The “fitch” of ",{"href":"?bref=Ezek.4.9","r":"Ezek.4.9","rawR":"Ezek.4.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezek.4.9","value":"Ezek.4.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezekiel 4:9"}," (",{"c":["nlt"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"}," “spelt”) is probably emmer, an inferior kind of wheat."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Plants_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Plants_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Plants_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Plants (Nutmeg Flower"},"; ",{"href":"?item=Spelt_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Spelt_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Spelt_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Spelt)"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Fitch","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Isaiah 28:25-27","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Isa.28.25-27","rawQueryValue":"Isa.28.25-27","sourceRefExact":"Isa.28.25-27"},{"anchorText":"Ezekiel 4:9","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezek.4.9","rawQueryValue":"Ezek.4.9","sourceRefExact":"Ezek.4.9"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"78c92302ac34675e6a2b0debf596444bbfb8ee5f257e189fb11106c9a46c4d6b","sourceItemName":"Fitch","sourceItemOrder":46,"sourceMember":"Article